      "id": "body_1",
      "label": "Answer",
      "default": "Chew one piece at a time using your back teeth (molars). Alternate sides every few minutes to train both sides evenly. Each session should last 10–15 minutes max. We recommend 3–4 pieces spread throughout the day. During your commute, at your desk, between sets — whenever.\n\nDon't overdo it. Your jaw is a muscle. You wouldn't do 6 hours of bicep curls. Same logic applies here. If you feel pain or discomfort, stop and rest. Build up gradually, especially in week one."
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Accordion 2"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "title_2",
      "label": "Title",
      "default": "Does it actually work?"
    },
    {
      "type": "textarea",
      "id": "body_2",
